course: dictionary
lesson: 11405
title: Accordingly: acting to fit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Accordingly» is a small word that links two things. It tells you that what comes next fits with what was just said. «Read the rules and act accordingly» means: read the rules first, then do what fits them.
explain: Think of it as "in the right way for this". If a sign says the road is closed, you take a different road, so you act accordingly. Ask yourself: what came just before this word, and what should follow from it?
explain: In formal writing, accordingly often means «so» or «therefore». «It rained all day; accordingly, the match was cancelled.» The rain is the reason and the cancelled match is the result. To check, swap in "so" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Accordingly means in a way that fits what has just been said or what is needed.
fact: In formal writing, accordingly can mean «so» or «therefore».
fact: Accordingly links a reason to a result.
fact: «Read the rules and act accordingly.» means: follow the rules when you act.
fact: Accordingly is an adverb, because it tells you how something is done.
exercise: «The sign said Wet floor, so Mia walked slowly and carefully. She acted accordingly.» What does acted accordingly mean here? | She went home for lunch | She ran as fast as she could | *She acted in a way that fit the sign | She ignored the sign completely
exercise: «It snowed all night; accordingly, the school was closed.» What does accordingly mean here? | Happily, with a song | *Therefore, because of the snow | Quietly, under the snow | Before the snow started
exercise: «The rules changed; accordingly, we changed our plan.» Which word means the same as accordingly here? | *Therefore | Yesterday | Slowly | Sadly
test: Jo read the recipe and measured the flour accordingly. What does accordingly suggest? | Eating the flour | *Measuring in the way the recipe says | Measuring with her eyes shut | Throwing the recipe away
test: «The forecast said heavy rain, so we took our coats; accordingly, we stayed dry.» Which word in the sentence shows the result? | forecast | *accordingly | coats | heavy
exam: «The bridge was closed; accordingly, we took the long road.» Which word could replace accordingly without changing the meaning? | Happily | Loudly | Yesterday | *Therefore
